flowchart TB
%% PLAN PIPELINE. Split from pipeline-planning.mmd.
%% Input: a task entry and the auto generated docs, from the document generation
%% pipeline.
%% One job: turn the tasks.json entry into a plan file.
%% Starts at "plan the task". Ends with a draft plan, back in document
%% generation, or with an exit.
%% Rules that apply everywhere, not steps:
%%   1. Every read and write of tasks.json is atomic.
%%   2. The planner reads the tasks.json entry and the docs, nothing else. That is
%%      why the review plan pipeline writes codex's notes into the entry before it
%%      sends the run back here: a bare retry would repeat the first plan's
%%      mistakes.
%%   3. A subagent cannot ask the user anything. CLARIFY is how the planner says
%%      it needs something it was not given - an answer, or a file the entry did
%%      not list. It goes back to document generation in UPDATE mode so the docs
%%      are rebuilt to cover it, then the planner runs again.
%%   4. A script that fails operationally exits the run as run-failed. The task is
%%      already active and a worktree already exists here, so the failures exit
%%      runs in full.
%% Box definitions where the name alone is not enough:
%%   what did the planner return?  - three outcomes: PLAN, CLARIFY, ERROR.
%%                                   ERROR is agent() returning null or garbage.
%% Exit types this pipeline can produce:
%%   agent-failed       - an agent returned nothing usable
%%   run-failed         - a script failed operationally
%% run-failed is deliberately not drawn as an edge out of every box. It can leave
%% ANY green box, so drawing it would add one edge per box and hide the flow.
%% The draft plan this pipeline emits is the input to the review plan pipeline.
%% The review plan pipeline re-enters here when codex does not accept the plan.

  DOCS_INPUT["Input: { brief, docs, codexNotes? }"] --> PLAN_THE_TASK
  PLAN_THE_TASK["plan the task"] --> WHAT_DID_THE_PLANNER_RETURN{"what did the planner return?"}
  WHAT_DID_THE_PLANNER_RETURN --> PLANNER_RETURNED_PLAN["PLAN"]
  WHAT_DID_THE_PLANNER_RETURN --> PLANNER_RETURNED_CLARIFY["CLARIFY"]
  WHAT_DID_THE_PLANNER_RETURN --> PLANNER_RETURNED_ERROR["ERROR"]

  PLANNER_RETURNED_PLAN --> REVIEW_PLAN_PIPELINE["review plan pipeline"]
  PLANNER_RETURNED_CLARIFY -- "docs mode: UPDATE" --> DOCUMENT_GENERATION_PIPELINE["document generation pipeline"]
  PLANNER_RETURNED_ERROR -- "exit type: agent-failed<br/>exit note: the agent returned<br/>nothing usable" --> EXIT_WORKFLOW

  EXIT_WORKFLOW["failures exit"]

  %% pass/nopass: green is the branch that keeps heading for the next pipeline,
  %% red is the branch that ends in an exit.
  classDef pipeline fill:#2f7d46,stroke:#1e5c31,color:#ffffff
  classDef agent fill:#e07b39,stroke:#a8541f,color:#1a1a1a
  classDef decision fill:#e0b400,stroke:#a88600,color:#1a1a1a
  classDef output fill:#3b6ea5,stroke:#254a70,color:#ffffff
  classDef fail fill:red,stroke:#254a70,color:#ffffff
  classDef pass fill:#2f7d46,stroke:#1e5c31,color:#ffffff
  classDef nopass fill:#a52a1e,stroke:#6d1a12,color:#ffffff
  class WHAT_DID_THE_PLANNER_RETURN decision
  class PLAN_THE_TASK agent
  class REVIEW_PLAN_PIPELINE,DOCUMENT_GENERATION_PIPELINE pipeline
  class PLANNER_RETURNED_PLAN,PLANNER_RETURNED_CLARIFY pass
  class PLANNER_RETURNED_ERROR nopass
  class EXIT_WORKFLOW fail
  class DOCS_INPUT output
